## Content referenced by this manifest

This repository ships no third-party source itself. It is a set of `repo`
manifests, so what it *references* determines what a `repo sync` fetches. The
projects below are listed for due-diligence purposes; each is governed by the
license of its own repository.

Eclipse-hosted, maintained by this project (`eclipse-oniro4openharmony`)
* `device_board_oniro`, `device_soc_oniro`, `vendor_oniro` — Apache-2.0
* `libhybris` — a fork of upstream libhybris carrying the OpenHarmony
  adaptation. Apache-2.0 AND BSD-2-Clause AND ISC AND MIT for the code its
  OpenHarmony build produces; see that repository's NOTICE, which also records
  the LGPL-2.1 Wayland backends that ship in its tree but are never compiled.
* `device_board_rpi`, `device_soc_broadcom`, `vendor_iscas` — Raspberry Pi
  board support, Apache-2.0, referenced from `chipsets/rpi/rpi.xml`. These
  carry committed third-party binaries (Broadcom/Raspberry Pi GPU firmware and
  prebuilt Mesa libraries); see their own repositories for the applicable
  terms.

Unmodified upstream OpenHarmony mirrors (`eclipse-oniro-mirrors`)
* ~479 repositories referenced by `ohos/ohos.xml` and `chipsets/dayu200`.
  Content is OpenAtom OpenHarmony's; each upstream repository carries its own
  `OAT.xml` license declaration.

Third-party projects fetched from their own upstreams
* `asmjit/asmjit` — Zlib — https://github.com/asmjit/asmjit
* `zyantific/zydis` — MIT — https://github.com/zyantific/zydis
* `zyantific/zycore-c` — MIT — https://github.com/zyantific/zycore-c
* `Halium/android-headers` — Apache-2.0 (Android Open Source Project headers)
  — https://github.com/Halium/android-headers

Projects fetched from gitcode.com/openharmony
* A small number of upstream OpenHarmony repositories that are too large to
  mirror are fetched directly from `gitcode.com/openharmony` rather than from
  `eclipse-oniro-mirrors`. They are upstream OpenAtom OpenHarmony content on
  the same terms as the mirrored repositories; the difference is only which
  server serves them.
